        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Strymon bazochii\n- Genera: the Hawaii target genus, the genus that yields silibinin\n- Places: Hawaii\n- Products: Silibinin\n\nFacts:\n- Strymon bazochii was introduced to Hawaii in 1902 to control a genus in Hawaii.\n- Silibinin was discovered in 1925 and is extracted from a different genus.\n- The genus targeted by Strymon bazochii in Hawaii has more species than the genus that yields silibinin.",
